WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Look at the large outlined pieces. The little bumps help bricks join; we are not counting bumps as pieces.

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Count all the equal pieces: one, two, three, four. Four tells us how the whole is divided.

3
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:35.000
The bottom number is four. Its name is denominator. It tells us there are four equal pieces in the whole.

4
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Now count the green pieces: one, two, three. Three goes on top. We call it the numerator.

5
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Read the fraction: three quarters. Three green pieces out of four equal pieces altogether.
